             are touched and RSS is counted in whole pages. -O1 drops the inlining heuristics and
             IPA passes of -O2, so code is similar in size and data are untouched. Watch the stack:
             -foptimize-sibling-calls is an -O2 pass, so tail recursion is NOT removed at -O1.
             Measured at N=20,000 (code/runtime-dominated), this bounds what the lever can ever
             save; the process floor alone is 1,088 KB. On an MMU-less microcontroller the image
             change (-504 B (-2.4%)) is paid in full in flash/RAM, which Linux demand paging hides.
             Hypothesis (NEUTRAL) refuted: worth a closer look in the report (check the image
             breakdown in builds.log and the phase snapshots in phases.csv).
