[A-04] Allocator policy: mmap threshold raised [pipeline/phased]    (suite: alloc)
  TEST      : Run the phased pipeline with GLIBC_TUNABLES=glibc.malloc.mmap_threshold=33554432 so
             that blocks up to 32 MB come from the brk heap instead of mmap.
  TESTING   : Does freeing memory actually give it back to the OS?
  HYPOTHESIS: INCREASES
  BASELINE  : default malloc               -O2  --mode=phased
  VARIANT   : mmap_threshold=32MB          -O2  --mode=phased  GLIBC_TUNABLES=glibc.malloc.mmap_threshold=33554432
  RESULTS   : metric                        baseline       variant   delta                   verdict
             max RSS (time -v)             138.4 MB      146.0 MB   +7,840 KB (+5.5%)       INCREASES (+/-709 KB)
             image text+data+bss            24.9 KB       24.9 KB   0 B (+0.0%)             NEUTRAL
             tracked heap peak            137.23 MB     137.22 MB   -11.5 KB (-0.0%)        NEUTRAL
             file on disk (info)            72.3 KB       72.3 KB
             minor faults (info)              9,861         9,372
             run time (info)                0.430 s       0.430 s
  OUTCOME   : INCREASES (resident)   hypothesis INCREASES -> CONFIRMED   output: identical
  MEANING   : 'mmap_threshold=32MB' raises max RSS (time -v) by 7,840 KB (5.5%) versus 'default
             malloc'. mmap'd blocks are unmapped on free(); brk-heap blocks are only returned if
             they sit at the top of the heap. 'Phased' code relies on free() releasing memory, so
             the allocator policy decides whether phasing works. At N=1,000,000 the baseline needs
             138.4 MB resident, so the change is 5.5% of what the Critter must provision.

