  VARIANT   : overlay+streaming            -O2  --mode=overlay --fit=streaming
  RESULTS   : metric                        baseline       variant   delta                   verdict
             max RSS (time -v)             153.5 MB       16.0 MB   -137.5 MB (-89.5%)      REDUCES (+/-786 KB)
             image text+data+bss            24.9 KB       24.9 KB   0 B (+0.0%)             NEUTRAL
             tracked heap peak            152.66 MB      15.27 MB   -137.39 MB (-90.0%)     REDUCES
             file on disk (info)            72.3 KB       72.3 KB
             minor faults (info)              9,861         1,079
             run time (info)                0.430 s       0.120 s
  OUTCOME   : REDUCES (resident)   hypothesis REDUCES -> CONFIRMED   output: identical
  MEANING   : 'overlay+streaming' lowers max RSS (time -v) by 137.5 MB (89.5%) versus 'concurrent'.
             Overlays can only reduce peak to the largest phase; to go lower you must shrink that
             phase. With the design matrix gone the peak falls to raw + scratch. At N=1,000,000 the
             baseline needs 153.5 MB resident, so the change is 89.5% of what the Critter must
             provision. Run time changed -72% (0.430 s -> 0.120 s): a memory/time trade-off to
             weigh, not ignore.
----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
[O-05] Single process -> one process per phase (exec overlay)    (suite: overlay)
  TEST      : Run acquire, clean and predict as three separate processes that hand data off through a
             file; peak = the largest of the three max RSS values.
  TESTING   : Does splitting the pipeline into processes (the OS version of an overlay) lower the
             peak?
  HYPOTHESIS: REDUCES
             process 1: acquire                            8,752 KB
             process 2: clean                               16.5 MB
             process 3: predict                            138.0 MB
             peak of staged processes                      138.0 MB
             single-process baseline                       153.5 MB   -15.5 MB (-10.1%)
  OUTCOME   : REDUCES (resident)   hypothesis REDUCES -> CONFIRMED   output: identical
  MEANING   : 'one process per phase' lowers max RSS (time -v) by 15.5 MB (10.1%) versus
             'concurrent'. Each process starts with an empty heap and returns everything at exit, so
             peak is the largest stage; the cost is file I/O and one process floor per stage. At
             N=1,000,000 the baseline needs 153.5 MB resident, so the change is 10.1% of what the
             Critter must provision.

####################################################################################################
# SUITE: STACK  --  Stack usage and stack budgets  (6 tests)
####################################################################################################
----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
[S-01] Solver workspace heap -> stack [compute]    (suite: stack)
  TEST      : Run the compute unit with --scratch=stack: the 8 KB system + 32 KB trajectory become
             locals.
  TESTING   : Where does moving a buffer from heap to stack show up?
  HYPOTHESIS: INCREASES
  BASELINE  : scratch=heap                 -O2
  VARIANT   : scratch=stack                -O2  --scratch=stack
  RESULTS   : metric                        baseline       variant   delta                   verdict
             max RSS (time -v)             4,144 KB      4,144 KB   0 KB (+0.0%)            NEUTRAL (+/-32 KB)
             image text+data+bss            62.3 KB       62.3 KB   0 B (+0.0%)             NEUTRAL
             tracked heap peak              2.78 MB       2.78 MB   0 B (+0.0%)             NEUTRAL
             stack high-water               7,312 B       47.4 KB   +40.3 KB (+563.9%)      INCREASES
             file on disk (info)            72.0 KB       72.0 KB
             minor faults (info)                283           282
             run time (info)                0.000 s       0.000 s
  OUTCOME   : INCREASES (stack only)   hypothesis INCREASES -> CONFIRMED   output: identical
  MEANING   : 'scratch=stack' raises stack high-water by 40.3 KB (563.9%) versus 'scratch=heap'.
             Resident memory on Linux did not move measurably because demand paging only charges
             pages that are touched and RSS is counted in whole pages. The bytes merely move: heap
             shrinks, stack grows by ~40 KB. With an 8 MB default stack this is invisible on Linux;
             on an RTOS task with a 4 KB stack it is a crash. Measured at N=20,000 (code/runtime-
             dominated), this bounds what the lever can ever save; the process floor alone is 1,088
             KB.
----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
