# SUITE: BUDGET  --  Hard memory budget (deployability)  (1 tests)
####################################################################################################
----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
[B-01] Which pipeline fits a 64 MB device?    (suite: budget)
  TEST      : Run each pipeline memory plan with the address-space rlimit set to 64 MB (N=1,000,000),
             emulating a small embedded Linux target.
  TESTING   : Pass/fail under a hard memory budget, the way the product would actually fail.
  RESULTS   : configuration                     result                                     max RSS
             concurrent/materialized           FAIL (OOM)                                       -
             phased/materialized               FAIL (OOM)                                       -
             overlay/materialized              FAIL (OOM)                                       -
             phased/streaming                  PASS                                       24.0 MB
             overlay/streaming                 PASS                                       16.0 MB
  OUTCOME   : PASS: phased/streaming, overlay/streaming   |   FAIL: concurrent/materialized,
             phased/materialized, overlay/materialized
  MEANING   : Of 5 configurations, 2 fit the limit. RLIMIT_AS caps virtual address space, so malloc
             returns NULL exactly as on a device without swap. A configuration either fits or it
             does not; there is no 'mostly fits' in an unattended machine room.

